  "title": "Task Operator (TO) for In-Context Learning",
  "summary": "In-context learning (ICL) enables language models to perform new tasks from demonstrations without weight updates, but it requires processing the full set of examples, resulting in inefficient deployments. Task Operator (TO) introduces an analytically derived update to the attention output projection, which significantly improves performance by capturing the transformation of attention heads. This method achieves the best overall performance among prior methods and narrows the gap between zero-shot inference and ICL.",
